<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- doctrine: doctorcre-v5-astra-integration-review -->
  <!--
    THE GATE ZERO SCHEDULER CANARY, AND IT IS WRITTEN DOWN UNINSTALLED.

    This agent is listed in DEFINITION_ONLY in lib/launchd_hold.py, so its
    PRESENCE in ~/Library/LaunchAgents is a drift finding until Joe removes it
    from that list deliberately. Activating a schedule is a human act; this
    file is the definition of what would be activated, in the repo, where the
    rest of the machine's config already lives.

    WHAT IT IS FOR. Gate Zero's fourth predecessor step,
    `step:scheduler-active-receipt`, asks whether the scheduler is really
    running. The reader that judges it lives in
    mcp-server/src/gate-zero-seam-readers.v5.js and wants an ops.run row whose
    evidence_ref is not null, written by bin/run-scheduled.sh, plus a later
    observation of that same run key and receipt. Nothing in the ledger could
    supply that: on 2026-09-11 production held 28,309 runs, 21,894 of them from
    this wrapper, and not one carrying an evidence_ref.

    WHY A DISTINCT RUN KEY. Every other wrapper-driven agent passes
    `launchd.run`, so the ledger cannot tell one job's dispatch from another's
    by key alone. This one passes `gatezero.canary`, which is the key the gate
    is pointed at and which nothing else writes.

    WHY NO OPTIONS AT ALL, and this is the correction PR #1006 review 1 forced.
    ProgramArguments below is exactly the wrapper's documented positional
    shape: the wrapper, the service key, the run key, and the command. THE
    WRAPPER MINTS THE RECEIPT ITSELF (PR #1002), from its own clock and the
    machine's own entropy, after the child exits; there is no receipt path to
    hand it and no variable that moves one. An earlier revision of this file
    passed a retired `evidence ref file` flag and a path, which the wrapper's
    option loop (bin/run-scheduled.sh lines 183 to 200) does NOT recognise:

        while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
          case "$1" in
            [heartbeat interval]) ... shift 2 ;;
            [also heartbeat])     ... shift 2 ;;
            [bare double hyphen]) shift; break ;;
            *) break ;;
          esac
        done

    An unknown flag hits the `*) break` arm, so it is not refused — it becomes
    $1, which the next two lines read as the SERVICE KEY, making the run key
    the receipt path and the command the word after it. The agent would have
    tried to execute `gate-zero-canary` as a program and recorded a failed run
    under a service nothing registers. The flag names are written in words
    rather than typed here because a double hyphen is illegal inside an XML
    comment, and writing one is what made notes-sweep the single plist in this
    directory no strict XML parser could read, found 2026-08-14 by
    tools/scheduler-truth.py.

    WHAT THE JOB ITSELF DOES: nothing, and exits 0. bin/gate-zero-canary.sh is
    a comment block and one `exit 0`, so the row this schedule produces is a
    statement about the scheduler and about nothing else.

    THE CADENCE IS HOURLY because the gate wants a recent dispatch, not a
    frequent one, and because every fire costs one spooled row. The service's
    declared grace in ops/config/services.json is sized for the 30-minute
    run-spool flush on top of that interval.
  -->
  <key>Label</key><string>com.carr.gate-zero-canary</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/bin/run-scheduled.sh</string>
    <string>gate-zero-canary</string>
    <string>gatezero.canary</string>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/bin/gate-zero-canary.sh</string>
  </array>

  <!-- carr-launchd-interval-seconds: 3600 | rendered by lib/launchd_calendar.py; macOS 27 launchd never fires StartInterval -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Minute</key><integer>43</integer></dict>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key><integer>60</integer>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>{{REPO}}/out/gate-zero-canary-launchd.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>{{REPO}}/out/gate-zero-canary-launchd.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
